# What the desktop opens once it is up: desktop_session's tail, with no FIFO and no polling. A desktop primitive is
# the compositor's, so it waits for the compositor to be up; these rules fire when it is.
# The person's list, moonwater desktop autostart, in its order (desktop_autostart).
rule autostart
	about "What the desktop opens when it is up"
	on service up compositor
	run autostart

# The on-screen keyboard, unless its setting is off: it starts hidden, and shows while a text field has the keys.
rule onscreen-keyboard
	on service up compositor
	if setting.keyboard.onscreen != off
	do open osk

# The installer on a boot from the stick: a verdict of live, or ask (a disk holds another build); never on an
# installed boot (desktop_installer).
rule installer
	about "The installer, on a live boot"
	on boot
	if $verdict != disk
	do open installer
